  "description": "Format large numbers into concise, human-readable strings (K, M, G, and custom tiers) for .NET apps, with optional binary (IEC) scaling, BigInteger support, culture-aware decimal separators, decomposition APIs, and Span-based formatting.",
  "id": "millify",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-04-19T21:48:13.933Z",
  "licenseUrl": "https://github.com/bolorundurowb/millify-dotnet/blob/master/LICENSE",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "6mOP9QYklsryhjAaWnForJMCYEQIHJjdj20MLjGaFqvY83qFjVGthhalEAo8IFrhgLb1kWKGxkwNo3lHa3/Yuw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 39785,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/bolorundurowb/millify-dotnet",
  "published": "2026-04-19T21:45:33.923Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Add optional trimming of insignificant fractional zeros (default on; set TrimInsignificantZeros=false to preserve fixed-width fractions).\n- Add SmartPrecision to reduce fractional digits for larger scaled magnitudes while keeping finer detail near 1–10.\n- Add MillifyScaleBase (decimal 1000 vs binary 1024) with IEC-style default suffixes for binary mode.\n- Add BigInteger Shorten/Decompose with exact decimal scaling when representable, plus a controlled overflow path.\n- Add CultureInfo support for the decimal separator only (digit grouping stays disabled).\n- Add MillifiedNumber plus Decompose/FormatScaled for split formatting workflows (tooltips, charts, a11y).\n- Add TryFormat overloads writing into Span (System.Memory referenced on netstandard1.6 and netstandard2.0).\n- Validate Units (non-empty, no null entries) on construction and when the Units property is set.\n- Fix incorrect casing logic that previously called ToUpperInvariant on the numeric text when Lowercase was true.",
